From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 12:21:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Read a block state property with one map lookup

BlockStateList.BlockData.get went through its ImmutableMap twice - containsKey
to decide whether to throw, then get to fetch the value - and then through
IBlockState.getValueClass().cast, a virtual call repeating a check the caller's
own cast already makes.

Every read of a block's level, age, facing or half pays this. A profile of the
saturating bench put it at 2.16% of the server thread, most of it under the
fluid flow scan, which asks for a water block's level several times per
neighbour.

An ImmutableMap cannot hold a null value, so a null from get answers exactly
what containsKey was asked. The unchecked cast is what the erased signature
hands every caller regardless: the checkcast the compiler inserts at the call
site is the same protection Class.cast was giving.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/BlockStateList.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/BlockStateList.java
index 10c8645bbb0dcf4d89689e2ea6add0a6cf72f899..0e8b5d1550aa8b2f94215a0534fd4fc15caac62e 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/BlockStateList.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/BlockStateList.java
@@ -113,13 +113,27 @@ public class BlockStateList {
             return Collections.unmodifiableCollection(this.properties.keySet());
         }
 
+        // Athena - one map lookup instead of two, and no reflective cast.
+        //
+        // Reading a property off a block state went through the map twice - containsKey to decide
+        // whether to throw, then get to fetch - and then through Class.cast, a virtual call that
+        // repeats a check the caller's own cast already makes. Every read of a block's level, age,
+        // facing or half pays this; a profile of the saturating bench put it at 2.16% of the server
+        // thread, most of it under the fluid flow scan.
+        //
+        // An ImmutableMap cannot hold a null value, so a null from get means the property is absent
+        // - exactly what containsKey was asked. The unchecked cast is what the erased signature
+        // gives every caller anyway: the checkcast the compiler inserts at the call site is the
+        // same protection Class.cast was providing.
         @Override
         public <T extends Comparable<T>> T get(IBlockState<T> iblockstate) {
-            if (!this.properties.containsKey(iblockstate)) {
+            Comparable comparable = this.properties.get(iblockstate);
+
+            if (comparable == null) {
                 throw new IllegalArgumentException("Cannot get property " + iblockstate + " as it does not exist in " + this.block.getBlockState());
-            } else {
-                return (T) (iblockstate.getValueClass().cast(this.properties.get(iblockstate)));
             }
+
+            return (T) comparable;
         }
 
         @Override
